<p>Hungary’s prime minister-elect Péter Magyar moved quickly on Wednesday to shape the post-election transition after his Tisza party’s landslide victory ended Viktor Orbán’s 16 years in power. Magyar said he wants the new parliament to convene in early May and a new government in place by mid-May. He also called on Hungary’s Orbán-aligned president to resign. At the same time, he vowed to suspend news broadcasts on state media until, in his view, conditions for objective and impartial reporting can be restored, framing the move as part of a broader effort to rebuild media freedom and public trust. The next question is whether Magyar can turn a sweeping electoral mandate into fast institutional change. Multiple reports say his supermajority would let him push constitutional and legal reforms affecting the judiciary, media, and other state institutions, while Brussels has already started talks aimed at unlocking more than €30 billion in frozen EU funds tied to rule-of-law concerns. The result has also drawn international attention because Orbán had become one of Europe’s most prominent nationalist leaders. President Trump and President Vladimir Putin both made supportive comments about Magyar despite previously backing Orbán, while European figures described the result as a possible opening for closer cooperation with the EU on governance and defense.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/c_nWyM0QKLsXM7wqSy7isuZG7HaQfRCpPhfVogEt3fVxL9CRXc7U5MsSXtRzZ1FExvOgbzWTvYjBuF2dmo2C30X9RePzcg3Z6qp_jNjILANTLMWS_Wh0rWndHUCYMAYB38ccmkaaKg7gsmzj83enEI87oVoPfcegoKYh4lFn8yHNwZFR4zCoMz2kUeM1DKAWMZb85x22I-mcP1s6b7nFQQ' alt='Peter Magyar campaigning in 2024 in Viktor Orban’s hometown, Felcsut, Hungary.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>EU funds: The European Commission is sending officials to Budapest on Friday to discuss reforms with Tisza figures as Magyar tries to unlock more than €30 billion in frozen funding, including roughly €10 billion in Covid recovery money that expires at the end of August.</li><li>Media reach: Politico reported that Orbán’s system gradually came to dominate about 80% of Hungary’s media landscape, leaving many rural voters reliant on coverage shaped by Fidesz-linked outlets.</li><li>Election driver: Several analyses said public anger over corruption and its effect on living standards played a central role in Fidesz’s defeat, with reports citing allegations of cronyism and misuse of public resources as potent campaign issues.</li><li>EU summit: Orbán will skip next week’s informal EU leaders’ meeting in Cyprus even though he remains caretaker prime minister until May, with another national leader expected to represent Hungary instead.</li></ul><blockquote>Every Hungarian deserves a public service media that broadcasts the truth. - Péter Magyar</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Péter Magyar: Magyar said state broadcasters should halt news operations until objective reporting standards are guaranteed, and he proposed a cross-party oversight body for public media with opposition access meeting &quot;BBC standards.&quot; (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/peter-magyar-first-target-hungary-state-controlled-media/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>European Commission: Commission President Ursula von der Leyen said the immediate priorities are restoring the rule of law, realigning Hungary with shared European values, and pursuing reforms that can unlock EU investment. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/commission-heads-hungary-budapest-friday-eu-funds-negotiations/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Kemi Badenoch: The UK Conservative leader argued that Orbán’s defeat shows right-wing populism is not necessarily durable if governments fail to deliver economic growth, and said Magyar’s rise reflects a reassertion of traditional center-right politics. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/badenoch-orbans-defeat-gives-me-hope-for-the-center-right/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The FT argued that Magyar has only a brief window to improve ties with Brussels and help fix EU dysfunction, especially on defense, before political momentum fades. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/8800d445-17d0-4927-a2e1-f6e00f839f8e'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Spiked: Spiked argued that progressive audiences should not assume Magyar represents a liberal turn, warning that his victory does not fit neatly into a simple left-versus-right narrative. (<a href='https://www.spiked-online.com/2026/04/15/peter-magyars-victory-is-nothing-for-progressives-to-cheer/'>Spiked</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350170/incoming-hungarian-leader-magyar-vows-suspend-state-news-broadcasts'>Incoming Hungarian leader Magyar vows to suspend state news broadcasts</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/8800d445-17d0-4927-a2e1-f6e00f839f8e'>Magyar is up against the clock in Hungary</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-what-s-next-for-peter-magyar-after-election-win/a-76785927'>Hungary: What&#x27;s next for Peter Magyar after election win?</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2ddd0xyl5o'>Magyar calls for fast handover of power in talks with Hungary&#x27;s president</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/badenoch-orbans-defeat-gives-me-hope-for-the-center-right/'>Badenoch: Orbán’s defeat gives me hope for center right</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/this-is-europe-end-of-orban-impact-on-european-elections'>Does Viktor Orbán’s defeat signal a wider backlash against ‘the forces of darkness’?</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.spiked-online.com/2026/04/15/peter-magyars-victory-is-nothing-for-progressives-to-cheer/'>Péter Magyar’s victory is nothing for ‘progressives’ to cheer</a> - spiked-online.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/hungarys-magyar-urges-president-to-quit-vows-to-overhaul-state-media'>Hungary’s Magyar urges president to quit, vows to overhaul state media</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-hungarian-leader-magyar-says-pro-orban-president-must-go/article70866123.ece'>New Hungarian leader Magyar says pro-Orban President must go</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/14/world/europe/viktor-orban-peter-magyar-election.html'>How Peter Magyar Defeated Viktor Orban, a Former Ally, In Hungary’s Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638466-orbans-exit-through-global-eyes/'>Orban’s exit through global eyes: Who really gains – and who doesn’t</a> - rt.com</li></ul>